WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.367
Need a small lookup table that is not in any file? Just type it!

2
00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:09.934
In this lesson, you will learn to create a table with Enter data, turn

3
00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:14.175
the first row into headers, and quickly undo a step that went wrong.

4
00:00:14.175 --> 00:00:15.480
Let's create one together!

5
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.866
On the Home tab, choose Enter data.

6
00:00:19.866 --> 00:00:21.275
A blank grid opens.

7
00:00:21.275 --> 00:00:22.685
I type two columns:

8
00:00:22.685 --> 00:00:26.560
Name and Gender, and then a few rows of example names.

9
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:45.953
Click OK, and the new query, called Demographic, appears in the Queries pane.

10
00:00:45.953 --> 00:00:52.560
Notice the headers are still Column1 and Column2, and our real headers sit in the first row.

11
00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:02.586
The fix:

12
00:01:02.586 --> 00:01:06.016
on the Home tab, click Use First Row as Headers.

13
00:01:06.016 --> 00:01:08.760
Now Name and Gender are proper column headers.

14
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.267
But watch what happens if you click it again by mistake:

15
00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:32.103
the first name becomes a header!

16
00:01:32.103 --> 00:01:33.940
Every click adds a new step.

17
00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:45.209
You can reverse it with Use Headers as First Row, which demotes the headers

18
00:01:45.209 --> 00:01:46.440
back into the data.

19
00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:01.518
Even simpler:

20
00:02:01.518 --> 00:02:04.914
go to Applied Steps and delete the step you don't need.

21
00:02:04.914 --> 00:02:08.620
Click the small X next to the step, and it is gone.

22
00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.956
Now the table is clean again, with Name and Gender as headers.

23
00:02:26.956 --> 00:02:29.660
Always check your headers before you move on.

24
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:43.884
Enter data is perfect for small lists, like regions, targets, or categories.

25
00:02:43.884 --> 00:02:45.960
Your own tables, in seconds!

